
# nodenv

nodenv is a version manager tool for the [Node.js][0] on Unix-like systems. It is useful for switching between
multiple Node.js versions on the same machine and for ensuring that each project you are working on always
runs on the correct Node.js version.

## usage

```shell
git clone "https://github.com/nodenv/nodenv.git" \
  ~/.nodenv
cd ~/dotfiles.git
git checkout dev && git pull
git submodule update --init
git submodule sync
stow -Rv nodenv
```

### homebrew

**NOTE:** This is the preferred method for MacOS; HomeBrew supports Linux as well, so it can
also be used in Linux if you so choose!

```shell
brew install nodenv -vd
```

### nodenv-installer
#### wget

```shell
wget -q https://github.com/nodenv/nodenv-installer/raw/HEAD/bin/nodenv-installer -O- | bash
```

#### curl

```shell
curl -fsSL https://github.com/nodenv/nodenv-installer/raw/HEAD/bin/nodenv-installer | bash
```

#### node-build

```shell
git clone https://github.com/nodenv/node-build.git "$(nodenv root).git"/plugins/node-build
```

